    "body": "Followup https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/39378\n\n### Problem\n\nWhen `:connect ssh://` fails for an ordinary reason (unknown or changed host key, auth failure, failed install, remote Nvim crash), the error shows up as `E5108: Lua: …` plus a full Lua traceback, followed by a second error, `E6101: SSH connection failed`.\n\n`ex_connect` calls `vim.net._ssh.start()` via `nlua_call_typval()`, which reports any Lua error as E5108 with a traceback. `start()` already re-raises with `error(msg, 0)`, but that doesn't prevent the traceback.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nA single error message, without a traceback, e.g.:\n\n    E6101: SSH connection failed: SSH tunnel exited before the remote Nvim was ready: Permission denied (publickey).\n\nPossible approach: `start()` returns the error message instead of raising it, and `ex_connect` shows it after the `E6101:` prefix. Note that `start()` already returns nil when the user declines the confirm prompt, so declined and failed need distinct return values.\n",
